\section{Write Constraints, Then Inspect Their Reach}

The following is an OpenSTA Tcl script with SDC timing commands. It assumes a characterized library whose time unit is the nanosecond, a mapped module \texttt{top}, and synchronous data ports \texttt{din} and \texttt{dout}. The I/O delays here are examples, not timing obligations inferred from RTL.

\begin{verbatim}
read_liberty slow.lib
read_verilog top_stdcell.v
link_design top
create_clock -name core -period 5.00 [get_ports clk]
set_clock_uncertainty -setup 0.20 [get_clocks core]
set_clock_uncertainty -hold  0.03 [get_clocks core]
set_input_delay  -clock core -max  1.0 [get_ports din]
set_input_delay  -clock core -min  0.2 [get_ports din]
set_output_delay -clock core -max  0.8 [get_ports dout]
set_output_delay -clock core -min -0.1 [get_ports dout]
check_setup
report_checks -path_delay min_max
\end{verbatim}

The \href{https://opensta.readthedocs.io/en/latest/Commands/}{OpenSTA command reference} documents these reports and the supported exceptions. The script is one view; signoff needs appropriate min and max corners, propagated clocks where applicable, and parasitics matching the final implementation. In particular, inspect \texttt{report\_checks} for the actual launch and capture clocks, and run the tool's unconstrained-path report: a port omitted from \texttt{get\_ports din} is not covered by the example merely because another port is. Check setup and hold even when the logic passed equivalence. A multicycle exception changes the checked edges and requires a real sampling protocol and a review of both setup and hold. A false-path exception just removes a check; it does not add a synchronizer or make a wire safe.

Absence of a shared clock does not mean absence of timing constraints. In Venkataramani and colleagues' asynchronous flow, bundled data goes with a matched control delay: the request must not arrive too early for the data. That is a relative-timing obligation, not the periodic setup calculation above. In either setting, optimization can improve only paths it models. Validate the constraints and their coverage before using a report to claim improvement.
